#X msg 110 626 apin_mapping?;
#X text 245 626 query mapping between analog port number and digital
pin. Analog messages are numbered 0 to 15 \, which traditionally refer
to the Arduino pins labeled A0 \, A1 \, A2 \, etc. However \, these
pis are actually configured using "normal" pin numbers in the pin mode
message \, and when those pins are used for non-analog functions. The
analog mapping query provides the information about which pins (as
used with Firmata's pin mode message) correspond to the analog channels.
Return sequence of messages like: [apin_mapping A# PIN#( \, where #
is number.;
#X msg 110 772 capabilities?;
#X text 245 772 query pin capabilities. Return sequence of messages
like: [pin_info PIN# MODE RESOLUTION( \, where # is pin number.;
#X msg 110 812 firmware?;
#X text 245 812 query firmata protocol version. Returns message like:
[firmware ARDUINO_FIRMWARE_NAME.ino MAJOR MINOR(.;
#X msg 110 852 pin_mode;
#X text 245 852 sets pin mode. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 875 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 875 PIN#: pin number. Тип: int. Минимальное значение: 0\.;
#X obj 255 898 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 898 MODE: pin mode. Тип: symbol. Разрешённые значения:
INPUT \, OUTPUT \, ANALOG \, PWM \, SERVO \, SHIFT \, I2C \, ONEWIRE
\, STEPPER \, ENCODER \, SERIAL \, PULLUP.;
#X msg 110 953 pin_state?;
#X text 245 953 query pin state. The pin state is any data written
to the pin (it is important to note that pin state != pin value). For
output modes (digital output \, PWM \, and Servo) \, the state is any
value that has been previously written to the pin. For input modes
\, typically the state is zero. However \, for digital inputs \, the
state is the status of the pull-up resistor which is 1 if enabled \,
0 if disabled. Returns message like [pin_state PIN# MODE state( \,
where # is pin number. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1097 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1097 PIN#: pin number. Тип: int.;
#X msg 110 1122 report_apin;
#X text 245 1122 turns on/off analog pin (A0-A6) value reporting. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1145 cnv 1 83 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1145 ANALOG_PIN: analog pin number. Тип: int.;
#X obj 255 1168 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1168 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates analog reporting \,
messages like [apin PIN# value( are returned every sampling interval
(by default 19ms). Тип: int. Разрешённые значения: 0 \, 1\.;
#X msg 110 1223 report_dport;
#X text 245 1223 turns on/off digital port value reporting. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1246 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1246 PORT#: digital port number. Port is a group of pins
\, port 0 refers pins 0-8\. Тип: int.;
#X obj 255 1284 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1284 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates digital port reporting
\, messages like [dport PORT# value( are returned only on pin value
change. Тип: int. Разрешённые значения: 0 \, 1\.;
#X msg 110 1339 samp_interval;
#X text 245 1339 sets sampling interval - how often analog data and
i2c data is reported to the client. The default for the arduino implementation
is 19ms. This means that every 19ms analog data will be reported and
any i2c devices with read continuous mode will be read. Аргументы:;
#X obj 255 1422 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 255 1422 TIME: time. Тип: int. Диапазон: 10…10000\. Единицы:
'ms'.;
